</figure>
<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also tested the effectiveness of DPH-F and DPH-JS on a larger 32B model and found them to be equally effective. As shown in Table <a href="#A5.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ E.1 32B Experiments for SQL ‣ Appendix E Additional Experiments ‣ The Choice of Divergence: A Neglected Key to Mitigating Diversity Collapse in Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable Reward" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, please note that a greedy score of 70.5 on the Bird dataset is already approaching the performance limit of open-source Single-Models<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://bird-bench.github.io/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://bird-bench.github.io/</a></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Error Bar</h3>

<figure id="A5.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.07430v1/error_bar_chart_from_csv.svg" id="A5.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/546;" width="548" height="546"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Error bar in Llama Sql. For each method in our Llama SQL experiments, we conducted three separate reinforcement learning training runs. We then selected the model that achieved the highest pass@16 score on the Bird.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Mean@k Metric for MATHEMATICAL REASONING TASK</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To verify that our reinforcement learning training was effective on the math tasks, we evaluated the performance using the mean@k metric in Table <a href="#A5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ E.3 Mean@k Metric for MATHEMATICAL REASONING TASK ‣ Appendix E Additional Experiments ‣ The Choice of Divergence: A Neglected Key to Mitigating Diversity Collapse in Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable Reward" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>The Mean@k metric for models trained on math datasets. To accelerate training, we filtered the DAPO-17k dataset for data with a Pass@8 score of 0. In the end, we trained Llama on 5.8k samples and Qwen on 10.2k samples.</figcaption>
